                <pb facs="0613" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.001C13/87: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moody</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Austin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-16">December 16, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received 12:40
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your wire 14th. I feel confident that Mr. Valls will make no attempt to have a
                    warrant of arrest served on General Calles when he passes through Texas en route
                    to Mexico.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dan Moody</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
